igin":[478.401,187.922],"font":"Helvetica-Bold","size":10.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"If yes, describe briefly:","bbox":[54.18906,205.20224,138.74704,213.70224],"origin":[54.18906,211.77002],"font":"Helvetica","size":8.5,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Not Completed","bbox":[54.1891,226.88522,110.87559,235.38522],"origin":[54.1891,233.453],"font":"Helvetica","size":8.5,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Scoring and Interpretation Information","bbox":[34.3465,255.43449,290.26645,269.43451],"origin":[34.3465,266.25201],"font":"Helvetica-Bold","size":14.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"For comprehensive information on the asQ, ","bbox":[91.0394,274.68954,305.62741,285.68954],"origin":[91.0394,283.18903],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"see here","bbox":[305.62701,274.69052,348.42801,285.69052],"origin":[305.62701,283.19],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#0000ff","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":".","bbox":[348.42899,274.69052,351.487,285.69052],"origin":[348.42899,283.19],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"asQ Scoring","bbox":[91.03998,298.89053,151.56197,309.89053],"origin":[91.03998,307.39001],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"The asQ is not scored on a numerical scale. There is no total score, and no percentile or","bbox":[91.03998,310.99051,520.84302,321.99051],"origin":[91.03998,319.48999],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"normative comparison applies. Each of the four core items is answered ‘Yes’ or ‘No’ and two","bbox":[91.03998,323.09052,539.763,334.09052],"origin":[91.03998,331.59],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"items carry conditional follow-ups:","bbox":[91.03998,335.19052,256.08395,346.19052],"origin":[91.03998,343.69],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"- Item 4 (\"Have you ever tried to kill yourself?\") — if endorsed 'Yes,' two follow up questions are","bbox":[91.03998,347.29053,554.22809,358.29053],"origin":[91.03998,355.79001],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"presented: a free-text field to enter when the most recent attempt occurred, and a categorical","bbox":[91.03998,359.39053,542.87616,370.39053],"origin":[91.03998,367.89001],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"selection recording it as either within the last 12 months or over one year ago.","bbox":[91.03998,371.49054,468.879,382.49054],"origin":[91.03998,379.99002],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"- Item 5, the acuity item — administered only when 'Yes' is endorsed to any of items 1 through 4.","bbox":[91.03998,383.59055,560.50922,394.59055],"origin":[91.03998,392.09003],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"If item 5 is endorsed 'Yes,' a free-text follow-up (\"Describe briefly\") is presented.","bbox":[91.03998,395.69055,479.02087,406.69055],"origin":[91.03998,404.19003],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"asQ Screen Result Categories","bbox":[91.03998,419.89056,239.59494,430.89056],"origin":[91.03998,428.39005],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"The asQ produces one of three results:","bbox":[91.03998,431.99057,281.80194,442.99057],"origin":[91.03998,440.49005],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"- A Negative screen is a ‘No’ response to all four core items (wish to be dead, perceived","bbox":[91.03998,444.09058,517.763,455.09058],"origin":[91.03998,452.59006],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"burdensomeness, active ideation, and past attempt). The 5th acuity item is not administered.","bbox":[91.03998,456.19058,541.02808,467.19058],"origin":[91.03998,464.69006],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"This outcome suggests that no elevated risk of suicide is detected.","bbox":[91.03998,468.29059,414.47299,479.29059],"origin":[91.03998,476.79007],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"- A Non-acute positive screen is a ‘Yes’ to one or more core items along with a ‘No’ to the fifth","bbox":[91.03998,480.39059,545.89001,491.39059],"origin":[91.03998,488.89008],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"(acuity) item. This outcome identifies potential suicide risk. Further clinical assessment (for","bbox":[91.03998,492.4906,530.55597,503.4906],"origin":[91.03998,500.99008],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"example, a suicide safety assessment) is generally indicated to clarify the level of risk and","bbox":[91.03998,504.59061,527.54205,515.59064],"origin":[91.03998,513.09009],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"determine next steps, guided by clinical judgment and a clinician's own protocols.","bbox":[91.03998,516.69061,485.64285,527.69061],"origin":[91.03998,525.19006],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"- An Acute positive screen is a ‘Yes’ to one or more core items and a ‘Yes’ to the fifth (acuity)","bbox":[91.03998,528.79065,542.22717,539.79065],"origin":[91.03998,537.2901],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"item. This outcome identifies imminent (acute) risk. This is the highest-priority screen result and","bbox":[91.03998,540.89069,554.40405,551.89069],"origin":[91.03998,549.39014],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"calls for an immediate response.","bbox":[91.03998,552.99066,249.37392,563.99066],"origin":[91.03998,561.49011],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"NIMH asQ Toolkit (www.nimh.nih.gov/asQ). Clinicians who would like more detailed guidance","bbox":[91.03998,577.19067,545.83502,588.19067],"origin":[91.03998,585.69012],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"on responding to each screen result can refer to the NIMH asQ Toolkit. It is a freely available","bbox":[91.03998,589.29071,541.62225,600.29071],"origin":[91.03998,597.79016],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"resource that outlines suggested next steps, along with administration scripts, screening","bbox":[91.03998,601.39069,519.00598,612.39069],"origin":[91.03998,609.89014],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"pathways for a range of settings, a Brief Suicide Safety Assessment (BSSA), and other","bbox":[91.03998,613.49066,513.51703,624.49066],"origin":[91.03998,621.99011],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"guidance. These materials may be used as they are, alongside existing processes, or as a","bbox":[91.03998,625.5907,530.01697,636.5907],"origin":[91.03998,634.09015],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"starting point for developing protocols.","bbox":[91.03998,637.69073,276.90692,648.69073],"origin":[91.03998,646.19019],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Item 4 Interpretation Considerations. The developers note that the single most common positive","bbox":[91.03998,661.89069,556.30713,672.89069],"origin":[91.03998,670.39014],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"presentation is a ‘Yes’ to the lifetime-attempt item alone, accounting for between a third and a","bbox":[91.03998,673.99072,545.31812,684.99072],"origin":[91.03998,682.49017],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"half of positive screens (IHSgov, 2025). Recency is therefore important to capture, as a remote","bbox":[91.03998,686.0907,552.01715,697.0907],"origin":[91.03998,694.59015],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"past attempt with no current ideation may carry a different clinical meaning from a recent one.","bbox":[91.03998,698.19073,545.28497,709.19073],"origin":[91.03998,706.69019],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Does a positive screen predict future suicide risk? Most research on the asQ shows that it","bbox":[91.03998,722.39069,526.93695,733.39069],"origin":[91.03998,730.89014],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"agrees with longer structured suicide risk assessments at the time of screening. A smaller body","bbox":[91.03998,734.49072,553.82117,745.49072],"origin":[91.03998,742.99017],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"of evidence goes further and shows that a positive asQ screen (i.e., a 'Yes' to any of the four","bbox":[91.03998,746.5907,540.36823,757.5907],"origin":[91.03998,755.09015],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Page 2 of 3","bbox":[510.23697,809.92743,561.38708,819.92743],"origin":[510.23697,817.65424],"font":"Helvetica","size":10.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]}],"tables":[{"bbox":[28.3465,141.73231,566.92977,241.79095],"rows":[["","","Yes","No",""],["5","IfpatientanswersYestoanyofQuestions#1through\n# 4 askth efollowi nga cu ityqu es tion:\n,\n5 A rey ouh avingtho ughts ofkillingyourselfrightnow?\n.","1","0",null],["","Ifyes describebriefly:\n,",null,null,null],["","NotCompleted",null,null,null]],"cells":[[28.3465,141.73231,49.37007,170.07889],[28.3465,170.07889,49.37007,198.42505],[28.3465,198.42505,49.37007,219.11399],[28.3465,219.11399,49.37007,241.79095],[49.37007,141.73231,257.9528,170.07889],[49.37007,170.07889,257.9528,198.42505],[49.37007,198.42505,566.92977,219.11399],[49.37007,219.11399,566.92977,241.79095],[257.9528,141.73231,406.772,170.07889],[257.9528,170.07889,406.772,198.42505],[406.772,141.73231,555.591,170.07889],[406.772,170.07889,555.591,198.42505],[555.591,141.73231,566.92977,198.42505]],"header":{"names":["","","Yes","No",""],"external":false,"bbox":[28.3465,141.73231,566.92977,198.42505]},"status":"geometry_extracted_column_semantics_require_review"}],"chartObservations":[]},{"pageId":"d7b0647370d8e_p3","documentSha256":"7b0647370d8e0a8c5596f61876d00a0ca7da54db59a5b4faf548c567f5ddd353","pageNumber":3,"text":[{"text":"Client Name","bbox":[66.3844,116.31287,135.73239,128.31287],"origin":[66.3844,125.58502],"font":"Helvetica-Bold","size":12.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Generic Jenny","bbox":[147.73239,116.56485,218.64937,127.56485],"origin":[147.73239,125.06433],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"core items, regardless of the acuity item) also predicts suicide-related outcomes later on. In a","bbox":[91.0395,143.16556,543.43646,154.16556],"origin":[91.0395,151.66504],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"paediatric emergency department study, the asQ identified 93% of the young people who went","bbox":[91.0395,155.26553,550.22363,166.26553],"origin":[91.0395,163.76501],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"on to return to the ED with a suicide-related problem within the following six months — including","bbox":[91.0395,167.36551,556.88959,178.36551],"origin":[91.0395,175.86499],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"many who had originally presented for something unrelated (Ballard et al., 2017). In a larger","bbox":[91.0395,179.46548,537.35364,190.46548],"origin":[91.0395,187.96497],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"study of 15,003 young people aged 8–18, those who screened positive were roughly five to","bbox":[91.0395,191.56546,533.7345,202.56546],"origin":[91.0395,200.06494],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"seven times more likely to have a later suicide-related hospital visit than those who screened","bbox":[91.0395,203.66544,541.61053,214.66544],"origin":[91.0395,212.16492],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"negative (hazard ratios of 4.8 to 6.8, depending on whether all patients or only selected patients","bbox":[91.0395,215.76541,556.35052,226.76541],"origin":[91.0395,224.26489],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"were screened; DeVylder et al., 2019). In other words, a positive asQ is not just an accurate","bbox":[91.0395,227.86539,537.35364,238.86539],"origin":[91.0395,236.36487],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"snapshot of current risk. It also flags young people at greater risk of suicide-related difficulties in","bbox":[91.0395,239.96536,556.29559,250.96536],"origin":[91.0395,248.46484],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"the months that follow. This predictive evidence currently comes from paediatric and emergency","bbox":[91.0395,252.06534,557.49457,263.06534],"origin":[91.0395,260.56482],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"settings, so it is strongest for youth in medical settings.","bbox":[91.0395,264.16531,356.98645,275.16531],"origin":[91.0395,272.66479],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"asQ Report of Results","bbox":[91.0395,288.36533,199.24648,299.36533],"origin":[91.0395,296.86481],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"On a single administration, the report presents the screen result as one of the three defined","bbox":[91.0395,300.4653,534.93365,311.4653],"origin":[91.0395,308.96478],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"categories (negative, non-acute positive, or acute positive). If the response to item 4 was ‘Yes,’","bbox":[91.0395,312.56528,552.02759,323.56528],"origin":[91.0395,321.06476],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"the results will note whether the most recent suicide attempt occurred within the last 12 months","bbox":[91.0395,324.66528,552.62158,335.66528],"origin":[91.0395,333.16476],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"or over a year ago.","bbox":[91.0395,336.76529,183.36247,347.76529],"origin":[91.0395,345.26477],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"On repeat administration, the report presents the current result in the same way. Additionally,","bbox":[91.0395,348.8653,543.45862,359.8653],"origin":[91.0395,357.36478],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"there is a display of screen results over time, plotting each administration as a discrete marker","bbox":[91.0395,360.9653,548.32062,371.9653],"origin":[91.0395,369.46478],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"so that shifts between negative, non-acute positive, and acute positive status are visible at a","bbox":[91.0395,373.06531,538.60748,384.06531],"origin":[91.0395,381.56479],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"glance. This graph serves as a record of risk status across screenings, ordered by acuity, rather","bbox":[91.0395,385.16531,556.88959,396.16531],"origin":[91.0395,393.66479],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"than as a measure of symptom change; no change score is calculated.","bbox":[91.0395,397.26532,435.26245,408.26532],"origin":[91.0395,405.7648],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Beyond the overall screen result, a review of individual item responses is important, in particular,","bbox":[91.0395,409.36533,559.93658,420.36533],"origin":[91.0395,417.86481],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"the free-text responses to items 4 and 5. Item 4's follow-up prompts (when the most recent","bbox":[91.0395,421.46533,530.88556,432.46533],"origin":[91.0395,429.96481],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"attempt occurred) and item 5's description of current suicidal thoughts provide context that the","bbox":[91.0395,433.56534,547.40753,444.56534],"origin":[91.0395,442.06482],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"screen category alone cannot convey, helping to establish acuity and determine appropriate","bbox":[91.0395,445.66534,537.37555,456.66534],"origin":[91.0395,454.16483],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"next steps.","bbox":[91.0395,457.76535,144.23549,468.76535],"origin":[91.0395,466.26483],"font":"Helvetica","size":11.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Powered by TCPDF (www.tcpdf.org)","bbox":[6.0,839.89209,22.17,840.89209],"origin":[6.0,840.66479],"font":"Helvetica","size":1.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]},{"text":"Page 3 of 3","bbox":[510.23599,809.92712,561.38611,819.92712],"origin":[510.23599,817.65393],"font":"Helvetica","size":10.0,"colour":"#000000","direction":[1.0,0.0]}],"tables":[],"chartObservations":[]}],"rasterRegions":[],"rasterTranscriptions":[],"removedFalseChartDetections":[]}
